{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-lovable"},{"type":"text","value":". Then call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lovableText"},{"type":"text","value":" with a model id such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/gemini-3.7-flash"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lovable AI Gateway sits in front of Google and OpenAI models. You use one project key. You do not set up a provider account."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Auth"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". Lovable creates this key for each Cloud project."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export LOVABLE_API_KEY=\"...\"","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also pass the key to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" factory:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst adapter = createLovableText(\n  \"google/gemini-3.7-flash\",\n  process.env.LOVABLE_API_KEY!,\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Lovable-API-Key"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"X-Lovable-AIG-SDK: tanstack-ai"},{"type":"text","value":". Calls go to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://ai.gateway.lovable.dev/v1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default adapter uses the OpenAI Responses API. Model ids use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai/"},{"type":"text","value":" form."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server."}]},{"type":"text","value":" An endpoint that streams the reply over SSE:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: lovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n    messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" hook as every other provider:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\"\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\")\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <strong>{message.role}</strong>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          if (!input.trim() || isLoading) return\n          sendMessage(input)\n          setInput(\"\")\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"chat-completions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Completions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ api: \"chat\" }"},{"type":"text","value":" when the model must talk to Chat Completions. The default is Responses."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: lovableText(\"openai/gpt-5.5\", { api: \"chat\" }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"api: \"responses\""},{"type":"text","value":" is the same as the default. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"api: \"chat-completions\""},{"type":"text","value":" is the same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"api: \"chat\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summarize","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: lovableSummarize(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n  text: \"The Fender Stratocaster is a versatile electric guitar.\",\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"images","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Images"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate a new image, or pass image parts to edit one. OpenAI image models also accept a mask part ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.role === \"mask\""},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: lovableImage(\"openai/gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench\",\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"video","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video jobs are async. Create a job, poll status, then fetch the MP4 URL. Clips last 4, 6, or 8 seconds. You can write "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"4\""},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"4s\""},{"type":"text","value":" (same forms for 6 and 8)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1080p and 4K clips are always 8 seconds. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"8s\""},{"type":"text","value":" counts as 8 seconds. 4K works only on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/veo-3.1-fast"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/veo-3.1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: lovableVideo(\"google/veo-3.1-lite\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench, slow camera push-in\",\n  duration: \"4s\",\n  size: \"1280x720\",\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then poll "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getVideoJobStatus"},{"type":"text","value":" with that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jobId"},{"type":"text","value":". When the job is complete, the result includes the MP4 URL."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass one image part in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" to animate a still frame."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"embeddings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: lovableEmbedding(\"google/gemini-embedding-2\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speech"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: lovableSpeech(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts\"),\n  text: \"Welcome to the guitar shop.\",\n  voice: \"nova\",\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst audio = await fetch(\"/voice-note.mp3\").then((response) => response.blob())\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: lovableTranscription(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe\"),\n  audio,\n  language: \"en\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.text)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"bring-your-own-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Users can paste a Lovable project key in the browser. Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lovableByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok"},{"type":"text","value":", not from the package main entry."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\nimport { lovableByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok\"\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, lovableByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(lovableByok)\n\n  const adapter = createLovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\", apiKey)\n  // ...\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the client store and a save UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a model id from the curated lists. TypeScript rejects an id that is not on a list."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/gemini-3.7-flash"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fast OpenAI: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai/gpt-5.5"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image, video, embeddings, and speech:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai/gpt-image-2"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/veo-3.1-lite"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embedding default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google/gemini-embedding-2"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speech default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The curated lists are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_CHAT_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_IMAGE_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_VIDEO_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_EMBEDDING_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_TTS_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LOVABLE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"429 Too Many Requests"},{"type":"text","value":": the workspace hit its request-per-minute limit."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"402 Payment Required"},{"type":"text","value":": the workspace is out of credits."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.lovable.dev/features/ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lovable AI features"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for models, credits, and rate limits."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"auth","text":"Auth","level":2},{"id":"chat","text":"Chat","level":2},{"id":"chat-completions","text":"Chat Completions","level":2},{"id":"summarize","text":"Summarize","level":2},{"id":"images","text":"Images","level":2},{"id":"video","text":"Video","level":2},{"id":"embeddings","text":"Embeddings","level":2},{"id":"speech","text":"Speech","level":2},{"id":"transcription","text":"Transcription","level":2},{"id":"bring-your-own-key","text":"Bring Your Own Key","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"errors","text":"Errors","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-lovable`. Then call `lovableText` with a model id such as `google/gemini-3.7-flash`.\n\nLovable AI Gateway sits in front of Google and OpenAI models. You use one project key. You do not set up a provider account.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nvue: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-lovable\npreact: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nangular: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-lovable\noctane: @tanstack/ai-lovable\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Auth\n\nSet `LOVABLE_API_KEY`. Lovable creates this key for each Cloud project.\n\n```bash\nexport LOVABLE_API_KEY=\"...\"\n```\n\nYou can also pass the key to a `create*` factory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst adapter = createLovableText(\n  \"google/gemini-3.7-flash\",\n  process.env.LOVABLE_API_KEY!,\n)\n```\n\nThe adapter sends `Authorization: Bearer`, `Lovable-API-Key`, and `X-Lovable-AIG-SDK: tanstack-ai`. Calls go to `https://ai.gateway.lovable.dev/v1`.\n\n## Chat\n\nThe default adapter uses the OpenAI Responses API. Model ids use the `google/` or `openai/` form.\n\n**Server.** An endpoint that streams the reply over SSE:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: lovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n    messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n**Client.** The same `useChat` hook as every other provider:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\"\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\")\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <strong>{message.role}</strong>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          if (!input.trim() || isLoading) return\n          sendMessage(input)\n          setInput(\"\")\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Chat Completions\n\nPass `{ api: \"chat\" }` when the model must talk to Chat Completions. The default is Responses.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: lovableText(\"openai/gpt-5.5\", { api: \"chat\" }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n})\n```\n\n`api: \"responses\"` is the same as the default. `api: \"chat-completions\"` is the same as `api: \"chat\"`.\n\n## Summarize\n\n```typescript\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: lovableSummarize(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n  text: \"The Fender Stratocaster is a versatile electric guitar.\",\n})\n```\n\n## Images\n\nGenerate a new image, or pass image parts to edit one. OpenAI image models also accept a mask part (`metadata.role === \"mask\"`).\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: lovableImage(\"openai/gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench\",\n})\n```\n\n## Video\n\nVideo jobs are async. Create a job, poll status, then fetch the MP4 URL. Clips last 4, 6, or 8 seconds. You can write `4`, `\"4\"`, or `\"4s\"` (same forms for 6 and 8).\n\n1080p and 4K clips are always 8 seconds. `\"8s\"` counts as 8 seconds. 4K works only on `google/veo-3.1-fast` and `google/veo-3.1`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: lovableVideo(\"google/veo-3.1-lite\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench, slow camera push-in\",\n  duration: \"4s\",\n  size: \"1280x720\",\n})\n```\n\nThen poll `getVideoJobStatus` with that `jobId`. When the job is complete, the result includes the MP4 URL.\n\nPass one image part in `prompt` to animate a still frame.\n\n## Embeddings\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: lovableEmbedding(\"google/gemini-embedding-2\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)\n```\n\n## Speech\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: lovableSpeech(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts\"),\n  text: \"Welcome to the guitar shop.\",\n  voice: \"nova\",\n})\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst audio = await fetch(\"/voice-note.mp3\").then((response) => response.blob())\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: lovableTranscription(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe\"),\n  audio,\n  language: \"en\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.text)\n```\n\n## Bring Your Own Key\n\nUsers can paste a Lovable project key in the browser. Import `lovableByok` from `@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok`, not from the package main entry.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\nimport { lovableByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok\"\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, lovableByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(lovableByok)\n\n  const adapter = createLovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\", apiKey)\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for the client store and a save UI.\n\n## Models\n\nPass a model id from the curated lists. TypeScript rejects an id that is not on a list.\n\nChat:\n\n- Default: `google/gemini-3.7-flash`\n- Fast OpenAI: `openai/gpt-5.5`\n\nImage, video, embeddings, and speech:\n\n- Image default: `openai/gpt-image-2`\n- Video default: `google/veo-3.1-lite`\n- Embedding default: `google/gemini-embedding-2`\n- Speech default: `openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts`\n- Transcription default: `openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe`\n\nThe curated lists are `LOVABLE_CHAT_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_IMAGE_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_VIDEO_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_EMBEDDING_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_TTS_MODELS`, and `LOVABLE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODELS`.\n\n## Errors\n\n- `429 Too Many Requests`: the workspace hit its request-per-minute limit.\n- `402 Payment Required`: the workspace is out of credits.\n\nSee [Lovable AI features](https://docs.lovable.dev/features/ai) for models, credits, and rate limits.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lovable AI Gateway\nid: lovable-adapter\ndescription: \"Use one Lovable API key to call Google and OpenAI models through Lovable AI Gateway. Chat, embeddings, image, video, speech, and transcription all work with @tanstack/ai-lovable.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - lovable\n  - ai gateway\n  - adapter\n  - chat\n  - responses\n  - embeddings\n  - image generation\n  - video generation\n  - tts\n  - transcription\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-lovable`. Then call `lovableText` with a model id such as `google/gemini-3.7-flash`.\n\nLovable AI Gateway sits in front of Google and OpenAI models. You use one project key. You do not set up a provider account.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nvue: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-lovable\npreact: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nangular: @tanstack/ai-lovable\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-lovable\noctane: @tanstack/ai-lovable\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Auth\n\nSet `LOVABLE_API_KEY`. Lovable creates this key for each Cloud project.\n\n```bash\nexport LOVABLE_API_KEY=\"...\"\n```\n\nYou can also pass the key to a `create*` factory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst adapter = createLovableText(\n  \"google/gemini-3.7-flash\",\n  process.env.LOVABLE_API_KEY!,\n)\n```\n\nThe adapter sends `Authorization: Bearer`, `Lovable-API-Key`, and `X-Lovable-AIG-SDK: tanstack-ai`. Calls go to `https://ai.gateway.lovable.dev/v1`.\n\n## Chat\n\nThe default adapter uses the OpenAI Responses API. Model ids use the `google/` or `openai/` form.\n\n**Server.** An endpoint that streams the reply over SSE:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: lovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n    messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n**Client.** The same `useChat` hook as every other provider:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\"\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\")\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <strong>{message.role}</strong>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault()\n          if (!input.trim() || isLoading) return\n          sendMessage(input)\n          setInput(\"\")\n        }}\n      >\n        <input value={input} onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)} />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={isLoading}>\n          Send\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Chat Completions\n\nPass `{ api: \"chat\" }` when the model must talk to Chat Completions. The default is Responses.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: lovableText(\"openai/gpt-5.5\", { api: \"chat\" }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n})\n```\n\n`api: \"responses\"` is the same as the default. `api: \"chat-completions\"` is the same as `api: \"chat\"`.\n\n## Summarize\n\n```typescript\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: lovableSummarize(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\"),\n  text: \"The Fender Stratocaster is a versatile electric guitar.\",\n})\n```\n\n## Images\n\nGenerate a new image, or pass image parts to edit one. OpenAI image models also accept a mask part (`metadata.role === \"mask\"`).\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: lovableImage(\"openai/gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench\",\n})\n```\n\n## Video\n\nVideo jobs are async. Create a job, poll status, then fetch the MP4 URL. Clips last 4, 6, or 8 seconds. You can write `4`, `\"4\"`, or `\"4s\"` (same forms for 6 and 8).\n\n1080p and 4K clips are always 8 seconds. `\"8s\"` counts as 8 seconds. 4K works only on `google/veo-3.1-fast` and `google/veo-3.1`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: lovableVideo(\"google/veo-3.1-lite\"),\n  prompt: \"a red guitar on a wooden bench, slow camera push-in\",\n  duration: \"4s\",\n  size: \"1280x720\",\n})\n```\n\nThen poll `getVideoJobStatus` with that `jobId`. When the job is complete, the result includes the MP4 URL.\n\nPass one image part in `prompt` to animate a still frame.\n\n## Embeddings\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: lovableEmbedding(\"google/gemini-embedding-2\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector)\n```\n\n## Speech\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: lovableSpeech(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts\"),\n  text: \"Welcome to the guitar shop.\",\n  voice: \"nova\",\n})\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { lovableTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\n\nconst audio = await fetch(\"/voice-note.mp3\").then((response) => response.blob())\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: lovableTranscription(\"openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe\"),\n  audio,\n  language: \"en\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.text)\n```\n\n## Bring Your Own Key\n\nUsers can paste a Lovable project key in the browser. Import `lovableByok` from `@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok`, not from the package main entry.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createLovableText } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable\"\nimport { lovableByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok\"\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\"\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, lovableByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(lovableByok)\n\n  const adapter = createLovableText(\"google/gemini-3.7-flash\", apiKey)\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for the client store and a save UI.\n\n## Models\n\nPass a model id from the curated lists. TypeScript rejects an id that is not on a list.\n\nChat:\n\n- Default: `google/gemini-3.7-flash`\n- Fast OpenAI: `openai/gpt-5.5`\n\nImage, video, embeddings, and speech:\n\n- Image default: `openai/gpt-image-2`\n- Video default: `google/veo-3.1-lite`\n- Embedding default: `google/gemini-embedding-2`\n- Speech default: `openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts`\n- Transcription default: `openai/gpt-4o-mini-transcribe`\n\nThe curated lists are `LOVABLE_CHAT_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_IMAGE_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_VIDEO_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_EMBEDDING_MODELS`, `LOVABLE_TTS_MODELS`, and `LOVABLE_TRANSCRIPTION_MODELS`.\n\n## Errors\n\n- `429 Too Many Requests`: the workspace hit its request-per-minute limit.\n- `402 Payment Required`: the workspace is out of credits.\n\nSee [Lovable AI features](https://docs.lovable.dev/features/ai) for models, credits, and rate limits.\n"}
